      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "Based on [[credential-scoping]], the Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment by **never storing it there at all**.\n\nHere\u0027s how it works:\n\n1. **A local secrets loader** reads the key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup\n2. **The key is injected only into the child process** \u2014 it\u0027s written directly into the environment of the spawned Ingest agent child process, immediately before that process starts\n3. **The Hub\u0027s own process environment remains unmodified** \u2014 it never holds the credential\n\nThis design means that even if the Hub process is compromised or misbehaves, it cannot leak the API key simply by inspecting its own environment variables, because the key never exists there. The credential lives only inside the short-lived child process that actually needs it to call the Anthropic API.\n\nThe Query agent follows the same scoping model\u2014it also receives the credential injected into its own child process environment at spawn time, not inherited from the Hub.",
